{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement","id":929856,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Traits of the Sidereal Exalted - Anima effects and Advancement","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-11T11:34:50-07:00","id":929856,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Traits of the Sidereal Exalted - Anima effects and Advancement","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anima Effects</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Sidereals instinctively have the following abilities by feeding 1 mote into their anima:</span></span><ul><li>She uses either version of the thaumaturgical ritual Read the Tea Leaves' (Exalted p. 490); she need not literally read tea leaves, but rather gains a brief insight into the intended future. If she consults the stars at night when using this power, she adds +3 non-charm dice to her (Perception + Occult) roll.</li> <li>The Sidereal learns the exact time of day in Creation. This functions even other realms, such as the Underworld, the Wyld, or Hell.</li> <li>The Sidereal may cause her caste mark to display itself as long as she desires.</li> <li>The Sidereal asks the Storyteller a single yes or no question, relating to her caste or kismet. She may only ask one such question a day.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chosen of Journeys Anima Effects</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>For 10 motes, the Sidereal invokes the Lesser Sign of Mercury upon herself or an ally out to Medium range. The Lesser Sign of Mercury adds (Essence) non-charm dice to all rolls depending on foot speed, mote notably rush, disengage and withdraw actions, for the remainder of the scene. When her anima is at bonfire/iconic, the Sidereal and all allies out to Medium range gain this benefit for free.</li> <li>For 7 motes, the Sidereal learns the direction to the nearest Heavenly Gate. If she is in a realm beyond Creation, it will direct her towards the most direct path back to Creation. The direction given is always in a straight line, without regard for geography or travelling abilities; if the Sidereal is trapped in a maze or on an island in the middle of the Great Western Ocean, this will not necessarily prove of tremendous value.</li> <li>At Essence 5, she gains the ability to invoke the Greater Sign of Mercury. Invoking the Greater Sign costs 30 motes and one permanent Willpower, transporting the Sidereal and any number of allies within Medium range to any known destination. The destination chosen need not be one the Sidereal has personally visited, but it must be unambiguously defined.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chosen of Serenity Anima Effects</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>For 10 motes, the Sidereal invokes the Lesser Sign of Venus upon herself or an ally out to Medium range. The Lesser Sign of Venus adds (Essence) non-charm dice to all instill and inspire actions she makes for the remainder of the scene. When her anima is at bonfire/iconic, the Sidereal and all allies out to Medium range gain this benefit for free.</li> <li>For 7 motes and 1 willpower, the Sidereal brings the peace of Venus to the scene. The first person who joins battle after this effect is invoked forfeits the base 3 initiative on the initial join battle roll. She may only invoke the peace of Venus once per scene, and only if no one has yet joined battle.</li> <li>At Essence 5, she gains the ability to invoke the Greater Sign of Venus. Invoking the Greater Sign costs 30 motes and one permanent Willpower, bringing a smothering peace to the scene. Taking any withering attack actions costs 1 initiative; taking any decisive attack actions costs 3 initiative. These costs must be paid before the attack is made. If, at any point, a round passes in which no characters take any attack actions, battle may not be rejoined during the rest of the scene.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chosen of Battles Anima Effects</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>For 10 motes, the Sidereal invokes the Lesser Sign of Mars upon herself or an ally out to Medium range. The Lesser Sign of Mars adds (Essence) as a non-charm bonus to her Soak and raises her Hardness to (Essence) if it is less than (Essence) for the remainder of the scene. When her anima is at bonfire/iconic, the Sidereal and all allies out to Medium range gain this benefit for free.</li> <li>For 7 motes, the Sidereal gains the blessing of Mars, forcing a reroll of a single attack taken against her or an ally. She may only invoke this blessing once per scene, and both she and her opponent must take the result of the reroll. Any Charms or other effects applied to the original attack apply to the reroll as well.</li> <li>At Essence 5, she gains the ability to invoke the Greater Sign of Mars. Invoking the Greater Sign costs 30 motes and one permanent Willpower. For the remainder of the scene, the target number of all damage rolls made against the Sidereal and her allies is increased by 1.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chosen of Secrets Anima Effects</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>For 10 motes, the Sidereal invokes the Lesser Sign of Jupiter upon herself or an ally out to Medium range. The Lesser Sign of Jupiter adds (Essence / 2, round up) as a non-charm bonus to her Resolve and Guile for the remainder of the scene. The thoughts of an individual under the Lesser Sign of Jupiter are also sacrosanct, and may not be directly perceived by any force or effect. When her anima is at bonfire/iconic, the Sidereal and all allies out to Medium range gain this benefit for free.</li> <li>For 7 motes, the Sidereal asks the Storyteller a second yes or no question relating to her caste or kismet.</li> <li>At Essence 5, she gains the ability to invoke the Greater Sign of Jupiter. Invoking the Greater Sign costs 30 motes and one permanent Willpower. All individuals in the current scene are treated as being inside of fate for all purposes, even if they could not normally exist inside of fate.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chosen of Endings Anima Effects</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>For 10 motes, the Sidereal invokes the Lesser Sign of Saturn upon herself or an ally out to Medium range. The Lesser Sign of Saturn adds (Essence / 2, round up) non-charm dice to the next decisive attack she makes. An individual may only benefit from the Lesser Sign of Saturn granted by a given Sidereal once per scene. If she has gained multiple such blessings in the same scene, then she uses the one which adds the most dice first. When her anima is at bonfire/iconic, the Sidereal and all allies out to Medium range gain this benefit for free.</li> <li>When the Sidereal lands a decisive blow which incapacitates or kills her target, she may spend 7 motes and 1 willpower to not reset to base initiative. She may only use this effects once per day.</li> <li>At Essence 5, she gains the ability to invoke the Greater Sign of Saturn. Invoking the Greater Sign costs 30 motes and one permanent Willpower. For the remainder of the scene, the target number for all decisive damage rolls made by the Sidereal and her allies is decreased by 1.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Character Advancement</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sidereals advance as Solars do, gaining five experience points per session, which players spend to increase characters\u2019 traits as well as to buy new Charms, save as noted below</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Experience Points</span></span></b><br /><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trait</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Experience Cost</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sidereal Charm</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">12 (10 if Caste or Favored)</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sidereal Martial Arts Charm</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">12</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Martial Arts Charm</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">10</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spell</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">12 (10 if Occult is a Caste or Favored Ability)</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">New Evocation</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">14</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sidereal Experience</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In addition to normal experience, characters can gain sidereal experience in each session. Sidereal experience may be spent on anything that except Sidereal Charms or Sidereal Martial Arts charms. Players have two opportunities to earn sidereal experience per session. They may earn up to one Destined Bonus and one Division Bonus, for a total of four sidereal experience per session.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Destined Bonus</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Characters can gain 2 points of sidereal experience by fulfilling any one of the following criteria per session:</span></span><ul><li>Expressing, supporting, or engaging with her kismet in such a way that it reveals something about the character, develops the character\u2019s personality, or provides a moment that everyone at the table enjoys.</li> <li>Being significantly challenged, endangered, or harmed in the course of pursuing her kismet.</li> <li>Being significantly challenged, impeded or endangered by a Flaw.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Division Bonus</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Characters can gain 2 points of sidereal experience by fulfilling any one of the following criteria per session:</span></span><ul><li>Intentionally ceding the spotlight of the scene\u2019s focus to another player\u2019s character in such a way that it makes that character shine.</li> <li>Chosen of Journeys: Guide someone you hold a Major or Defining Tie towards, or act as a guide in the service of a Major or Defining Principle, through dangerous territory. Encourage someone to undertake a significant or life-altering journey. Get into significant trouble by being the bearer of bad news.</li> <li>Chosen of Serenity: Develop a new, mutual, positive Defining Tie between yourself and another, or between any two people. Successfully conclude a significant conflict without violence. Suffer great hardship in the service to a positive Major or Defining Tie.</li> <li>Chosen of Battles: Overcome a challenge to a Major or Defining Intimacy by violence. Encourage someone to strike back against an oppressor- this need not be violent, but must be a significant or life-altering task. Survive great danger or hardship in the service of a Major or Defining Principle.</li> <li>Chosen of Secrets: Reveal or conceal a secret of significant interest to another player\u2019s character. Learn a significant secret at great personal risk. Persuade someone to take a significant or life-altering task or risk, while withholding some critical piece of information.</li> <li>Chosen of Endings: Witness the end of someone or something you hold a Major or Defining Intimacy towards. Weaken a Major or Defining Intimacy while performing your duty. Foster the start of a new beginning after an ending.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Training Times</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sidereal Exalted train at the same speed at Solars, save as noted below:</span></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trait</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Training Time</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wushu Martial Arts Charm</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Essence minimum) days</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sidereal Martial Arts Charm</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Essence minimum) weeks</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">New Evocation</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Essence minimum) weeks</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T11:55:00-07:00","id":929870,"title":"","content":"List of thoughts (mostly questions)<ul><li>I like the Anima effects. For some reason, I always had the idea that since Sidereals were based on the movements of the stars, that instead of the time of day, they should be able to know the time of the year, aka <i>the Date</i>. That would be cool instead of the time of day. My 2 cents.</li> <li>Do you think this &quot;can ask one yes/no question once per day&quot; thing can be used to abuse by a player? It feels very open ended and very strong. It doesn't seem to list any restrictions or even the Storyteller having the power of veto or vagueity.</li> <li>Why did you choose to retain spending a Permanent Willpower to invoke Greater Signs? It was one of the features in previous editions that made me never use them except for NPCs which never needed to care again. Seems like this edition's reset condition philosophy could easily be applied here instead without so harshly punishing a character.</li> <li>Why did you stick with Sidereal's buying things more expensively? That feels like an odd artifact from previous editions that I'm not convinced needs to remain. Especially with the vast number of charms you still have for them, it doesn't need to be balanced against the Solar's number anymore, imo. I kind of like that Evocations are more expensive, but not seeing why Charms and such are still.</li> <li>Your Division bonus for Sidereal Experience feels pretty harsh. The Solar Caste criteria seems <i>mostly</i> doable almost every session without a lot of difficulty, but the ones here feel like once every 3-4 sessions likely. Is that intentional? Am I off-base? Making everything surrounding a &quot;significant event&quot; or a &quot;Major or Defining Intimacy&quot; makes it feel very rigid.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T12:20:54-07:00","id":929888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement?p=929870#post929870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">List of thoughts (mostly questions)<ul><li>I like the Anima effects. For some reason, I always had the idea that since Sidereals were based on the movements of the stars, that instead of the time of day, they should be able to know the time of the year, aka <i>the Date</i>. That would be cool instead of the time of day. My 2 cents.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>This was actually my initial impulse as well- but I decided that the number of times that the player would want to know the exact *date* as opposed to exact *time of day* would be significantly more limited, and significantly easier to discover via non-magical means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement?p=929870#post929870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Do you think this &quot;can ask one yes/no question once per day&quot; thing can be used to abuse by a player? It feels very open ended and very strong. It doesn't seem to list any restrictions or even the Storyteller having the power of veto or vagueity.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>It's a concern, but I'm inclined to think that the 'related to caste or kismet' and binary yes/no questions are enough of a safeguard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement?p=929870#post929870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Why did you choose to retain spending a Permanent Willpower to invoke Greater Signs? It was one of the features in previous editions that made me never use them except for NPCs which never needed to care again. Seems like this edition's reset condition philosophy could easily be applied here instead without so harshly punishing a character.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, the Greater Signs cost a permanent *Essence* previously, which was an insane cost. A permanent willpower is, what, 8xp? It's still staggeringly expensive, but I believe that Sidereals having means to perform staggering sacrifices for great albiet temporary power boosts is very in their thematic wheelhouse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement?p=929870#post929870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Why did you stick with Sidereal's buying things more expensively? That feels like an odd artifact from previous editions that I'm not convinced needs to remain. Especially with the vast number of charms you still have for them, it doesn't need to be balanced against the Solar's number anymore, imo. I kind of like that Evocations are more expensive, but not seeing why Charms and such are still.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Training times and BP/XP were also relatively unpopular and widely regarded as an odd artifact from previous editions; I expect variant experience costs by exaltation to continue to exist, as a means of expressing Solar power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement?p=929870#post929870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Your Division bonus for Sidereal Experience feels pretty harsh. The Solar Caste criteria seems <i>mostly</i> doable almost every session without a lot of difficulty, but the ones here feel like once every 3-4 sessions likely. Is that intentional? Am I off-base? Making everything surrounding a &quot;significant event&quot; or a &quot;Major or Defining Intimacy&quot; makes it feel very rigid.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno; to me, they feel roughly comparable. I mean, the Solar Role bonuses almost all have the 'Major or Defining intimacy' or 'significant effort' type clauses as well. They *might* be more narrow, because the Sidereals tend to represent narrower thematic spaces. OTOH, the missions from the Bureau of Heaven *should* generally be giving them plenty of chances to trip those triggers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T12:31:09-07:00","id":929893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement?p=929888#post929888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was actually my initial impulse as well- but I decided that the number of times that the player would want to know the exact *date* as opposed to exact *time of day* would be significantly more limited, and significantly easier to discover via non-magical means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because it's more useful doesn't make it better design. I say go for the interesting one!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement?p=929888#post929888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a concern, but I'm inclined to think that the 'related to caste or kismet' and binary yes/no questions are enough of a safeguard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that depends on how much the ST wants the party to have to <i>work</i> to accomplish their Kismet. But fair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement?p=929888#post929888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, the Greater Signs cost a permanent *Essence* previously, which was an insane cost. A permanent willpower is, what, 8xp? It's still staggeringly expensive, but I believe that Sidereals having means to perform staggering sacrifices for great albiet temporary power boosts is very in their thematic wheelhouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed the fact that Willpower was cheap to buy. That's a valid point. I'd still prefer an interesting (maybe even difficult) reset condition, but your method is valid at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement?p=929888#post929888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Training times and BP/XP were also relatively unpopular and widely regarded as an odd artifact from previous editions; I expect variant experience costs by exaltation to continue to exist, as a means of expressing Solar power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it could still be that way (though training times have been played down a lot, with emphasis on &quot;use what makes sense at your table&quot; which did not exist previously) but as long as people are homebrewing, I assume that they'll make a thing work the way they thing it should be (since it all gets invalidated later on, and it's easy to fix the xp cost thing when the book comes out). I guess I'm just saying don't do it because you think it'll be that way later, do it because you think it's how it should be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement?p=929888#post929888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno; to me, they feel roughly comparable. I mean, the Solar Role bonuses almost all have the 'Major or Defining intimacy' or 'significant effort' type clauses as well. They *might* be more narrow, because the Sidereals tend to represent narrower thematic spaces. OTOH, the missions from the Bureau of Heaven *should* generally be giving them plenty of chances to trip those triggers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ran out of time but I plan to come back to this one again. I have thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T12:31:25-07:00","id":929894,"title":"","content":"The ask one question is very over powered. I know Sidereals are suppose to know things, but they have charms for that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T12:36:38-07:00","id":929897,"title":"","content":"Hm.<br /> <br /> Could folks describe a yes/no question that they believe would reduce the fun of the game, and which would fit within a caste role?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T12:59:54-07:00","id":929914,"title":"","content":"I agree that the question effects are much too powerful for just 1 mote. The first and the last one are also somewhat redundant, I would combine it: They can make one vague &quot;tea leaves&quot; style question relating to her caste or kismet. This makes it more fun for players because they could get a vague answer about what the ST is planning without asking a yes / no question that could derail things, or just constantly spamming the first effect to amass information.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12025,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","user":"PraxisCat","date":".  I was wrong and dumb 07-11-2016, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:02:08-07:00","id":929917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PraxisCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement?p=929914#post929914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other note You use &quot;target numbers&quot; relating to damage rolls in a number of places. Damage rolls don't have target numbers: They deal their successes unless the die they're rolling are lower than Hardness. I think you mean attack rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Damage rolls don't have Difficulties, they do have a Target Number (generally 7). That means that every die that comes up a 7 or higher is a success. By raising that TN, you would make only 8+ a success, while lowering it would make 6+ a success (or what have you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:05:35-07:00","id":929920,"title":"","content":"Make it once per story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:09:42-07:00","id":929923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement?p=929917#post929917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Damage rolls don't have Difficulties, they do have a Target Number (generally 7). That means that every die that comes up a 7 or higher is a success. By raising that TN, you would make only 8+ a success, while lowering it would make 6+ a success (or what have you).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I completely misunderstood what it meant by target number, my bad! Edited out my goof.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:15:11-07:00","id":929927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement?p=929920#post929920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make it once per story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting thought; I'd still like to see an example of a game derailing yes/no question.<br /> <br /> (I mean- in some cases, *yes* it can cut through mystery like a knife through hot butter by letting you definitely eliminate a potential false trail. I'm... kind of alright with a Sidereal being able to say 'Look, I know all the evidence points at that thing, but trust me, I know the thing, and that is not the thing')","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:48:49-07:00","id":929946,"title":"","content":"The Yes/no is fine with an added st veto, with advice to only use it sparingly... let the fate ninja pull that kind of shenanigan. <br /> <br /> The perm willpower is a no-no in my book. Anything that permanently eats character XP is to me abominable. Make it 2wp + once per story","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T14:24:07-07:00","id":929967,"title":"","content":"Most of my qualms are with their Kismet, where it's supposed to be this character defining story arc, but it feels like it could be distilled in a few days. There's no mystery when you can ask questions that are perfectly truthful.<br /> <br /> As far as castes, I think it all comes down to the chosen of Secrets. &quot;Is the Scarlet Empress still in Creation?&quot; Since no one knows, it feels pretty within my caste to find out. Each day narrow it down location by location until I find out the story piece that few STs really want to deal with. &quot;Is the Mask of Winters able to be killed?&quot; Then start whiddling down options.<br /> <br /> I've met very few people who can't solve a problem with a game of 20 Questions. Once per day means that any problem of any scale could potentially be resolved in less than a month.<br /> <br /> If that's not a problem to you, then there's no problem. But some of us have been in games where players find the most clever/obtuse ways to use Ask a Question, Get an Answer kind of powers. Though at least it's not Efficient Secretary Technique...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T19:06:07-07:00","id":930103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement?p=929946#post929946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Yes/no is fine with an added st veto, with advice to only use it sparingly... let the fate ninja pull that kind of shenanigan.<br /> <br /> The perm willpower is a no-no in my book. Anything that permanently eats character XP is to me abominable. Make it 2wp + once per story</div> </div> </div> </div>At 'Once a story', the cost is basically immaterial unless it's permanent.<br /> Hm.<br /> <br /> What if the willpower and motes *stay* spent for the remainder of the story? (In that case, I'd knock the cost back to 20m) They'll still recover in time, but they're effectively locked away for quite some time?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T19:10:31-07:00","id":930108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement?p=929967#post929967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of my qualms are with their Kismet, where it's supposed to be this character defining story arc, but it feels like it could be distilled in a few days. There's no mystery when you can ask questions that are perfectly truthful.<br /> <br /> As far as castes, I think it all comes down to the chosen of Secrets. &quot;Is the Scarlet Empress still in Creation?&quot; Since no one knows, it feels pretty within my caste to find out. Each day narrow it down location by location until I find out the story piece that few STs really want to deal with. &quot;Is the Mask of Winters able to be killed?&quot; Then start whiddling down options.<br /> <br /> I've met very few people who can't solve a problem with a game of 20 Questions. Once per day means that any problem of any scale could potentially be resolved in less than a month.<br /> <br /> If that's not a problem to you, then there's no problem. But some of us have been in games where players find the most clever/obtuse ways to use Ask a Question, Get an Answer kind of powers. Though at least it's not Efficient Secretary Technique...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those are excellent points. Especially with regards to the Chosen of Secrets- I mean, I could semantically argue the difference between a secret and a mystery, but...<br /> Making it pertain to only kismet, or only the intersection of kismet and caste, also doesn't solve; the same game of twenty questions could arise from a Chosen of Secrets with a kismet to discover the fate of the Scarlet Empress.<br /> <br /> I think the story duration might be good in that case- but with a slightly looser wording than 'yes or no'.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Sidereal asks the Storyteller a question, relating to her caste or kismet. She may only ask one such question per story. The answer must be a single word, which may not contain any proper names or title.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","user":"wastevens","date":". 07-11-2016, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T21:37:41-07:00","id":930165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/929856-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-anima-effects-and-advancement?p=930103#post930103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At 'Once a story', the cost is basically immaterial unless it's permanent.<br /> Hm.<br /> <br /> What if the willpower and motes *stay* spent for the remainder of the story? (In that case, I'd knock the cost back to 20m) They'll still recover in time, but they're effectively locked away for quite some time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T07:02:14-07:00","id":930308,"title":"","content":"How's that? (Other benefit; consolidating the costs into one spot saved some words)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar32_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"32\" data-vbnamecard=\"32\">Synapse</a><br /> <br /> <b>\u200bThe Greater Signs</b><br /> <br /> At Essence 4, Sidereals gain the ability to invoke the Greater Signs of their respective Maidens. These are tremendously powerful workings, and can scar the very soul of the Sidereal who draws upon them. The first invocation of the Greater Sign during a story costs 20 motes and 2 willpower, which may not be recovered until the story is concluded. Invoking the Sign additional times within the same story costs 1 permanent willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T07:06:14-07:00","id":930309,"title":"","content":"I think this is a nice compromise. I'd go with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T10:13:26-07:00","id":930399,"title":"","content":"Sure!<br /> Also 10 characters requirement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}